# Frontend

- The frontend is one web application. Staff open it in a browser on a phone, tablet, PC, or TV.
- Write it in TypeScript. The browser receives the JavaScript produced from that TypeScript.
- Build the screens with React. TypeScript is the language. React is the UI library.
- Use one responsive layout that stays readable and operable from a phone screen to a TV.
- User-visible strings live in `frontend/src/i18n.ts`.
- Follow the design template in `frontend/src/index.css`. Color, type, spacing, radius, and control styles are tokens in that file.
- Reuse the template classes for buttons, fields, panels, and alerts. A widget does not invent its own colors, spacing, or radius.
- Add a color to the template first, then use it. A screen does not introduce a one-off color.
- UI dependencies stay free and open source.
- Navigation uses the History API in `App`. Do not add a routing library, a CSS framework, or another UI library.

## Input

- Check a phone, an email, a username, and a password on the screen before the request. The backend refuses the same value.
- A customer phone is required. An empty email is allowed.
- A phone may contain digits, spaces, parentheses, `+`, and hyphens. Any other character is refused. Store the digits only. Remove a leading `0090`, a leading `90`, and a single leading `0` when they stand in front of the same 10-digit number, including a trunk `0` after `90`. The stored phone is 10 to 15 digits.
- An email has one `@`, no spaces, and a dot in the domain.
- A username this screen sets is required and at most 64 characters. A password this screen sets is 8 to 72 characters. An empty new password on an existing user leaves the password unchanged.
- Login does not say which of the username or the password failed.
- A name, brand, model, serial number, note, or search box has no character format. A required one is still refused when it is empty or only spaces.
- The checks live in one module. The screen names the field. The words are in `i18n.ts`, in English and Turkish.
